// Production golden set: software-testing course (ISYS2092/SYS3397) in cter-index-production.
// Questions are paraphrased from the local copies in documents-vault/; ISTQB sample exams are not covered (no local ground truth).
{"id":"fund-principle-01","question":"Why can't a test run ever prove that an application is completely bug-free, and which testing principle describes this?","expected_sources":["software-tesing-ISYS2092-SYS3397/Chapter 1 - Testing Fundamentals/Chapter 1 - Testing Fundamentals.md"],"key_points":["testing can show that defects are present","testing cannot prove that the software has no defects"],"answerable":true}
{"id":"fund-process-01","question":"Quy trình kiểm thử cơ bản theo ISTQB gồm những giai đoạn nào, và ở giai đoạn kết thúc kiểm thử thì nhóm cần làm gì?","expected_sources":["software-tesing-ISYS2092-SYS3397/Chapter 1 - Testing Fundamentals/Chapter 1 - Testing Fundamentals.md"],"key_points":["planning and control, analysis and design, implementation and execution, evaluating exit criteria and reporting, test closure","test closure makes sure all bug tickets are closed or resolved","testware is archived for later reuse","the team holds a lessons-learned review"],"answerable":true}
{"id":"fund-risk-01","question":"What separates a project risk from a product risk in testing? Give an example of each.","expected_sources":["software-tesing-ISYS2092-SYS3397/Chapter 1 - Testing Fundamentals/Chapter 1 - Testing Fundamentals.md"],"key_points":["project risks concern managing the project: people, time, budget, environment","product risks concern the quality of the software itself","e.g. the only tester falls sick or the staging server is down is a project risk","e.g. wrong interest calculation or a crash under heavy load is a product risk"],"answerable":true}
{"id":"sdlc-practices-01","question":"Theo ISTQB, khi kiểm thử trong bất kỳ mô hình phát triển nào thì nên áp dụng những thực hành tốt chung nào?","expected_sources":["software-tesing-ISYS2092-SYS3397/Chapter - 2 - Testing throughout SDLC/01 - Testing throughout SDLC.md"],"key_points":["each test level has its own specific objectives","every development activity has a corresponding test activity","test analysis and design start early (shift-left)","testers take part in reviewing documents such as user requirements"],"answerable":true}
{"id":"sdlc-vmodel-01","question":"In the V-model, which test level is paired with requirements definition, system analysis, design and coding respectively?","expected_sources":["software-tesing-ISYS2092-SYS3397/Chapter - 2 - Testing throughout SDLC/01 - Testing throughout SDLC.md","software-tesing-ISYS2092-SYS3397/Chapter - 2 - Testing throughout SDLC/02 - Test Levels.md"],"key_points":["user requirements map to acceptance testing","system analysis or system requirements map to system testing","design maps to integration testing","coding maps to component or unit testing"],"answerable":true}
{"id":"levels-vs-types-01","question":"How is a test level different from a test type, and can a test type such as regression testing be used at more than one level?","expected_sources":["software-tesing-ISYS2092-SYS3397/Chapter - 2 - Testing throughout SDLC/02 - Test Levels.md"],"key_points":["a test level is a group of test activities organised and managed together with specific responsibilities","a test type focuses on a particular quality characteristic or objective","functional, white-box and confirmation/regression testing can be applied at all test levels"],"answerable":true}
{"id":"levels-acceptance-01","question":"Who usually carries out acceptance testing, what is its goal, and what forms can it take?","expected_sources":["software-tesing-ISYS2092-SYS3397/Chapter - 2 - Testing throughout SDLC/02 - Test Levels.md"],"key_points":["mainly performed by customers or users","goal is to build confidence that the system fits the real business process","forms include UAT, OAT, alpha and beta testing"],"answerable":true}
{"id":"maintenance-01","question":"Once software is already in production, what situations trigger maintenance testing and what should that testing cover?","expected_sources":["software-tesing-ISYS2092-SYS3397/Chapter - 2 - Testing throughout SDLC/03 - Maintanance Testing.md"],"key_points":["triggers are modification, migration and retirement","the changes themselves are tested directly","regression testing of other parts based on impact analysis and risk","retirement needs data migration and archiving"],"answerable":true}
{"id":"static-vs-dynamic-01","question":"Is static testing a test level or a test type? How does it differ from dynamic testing?","expected_sources":["software-tesing-ISYS2092-SYS3397/Chapter 3 - Static Testings/Chapter 03 Static Testing.md"],"key_points":["static testing finds defects in documents, models or code without executing the code","dynamic testing runs the software to cause failures and then localises the defect","static testing is neither a level nor a type; it is an approach applied at every level"],"answerable":true}
{"id":"static-reviews-01","question":"Sắp xếp các hình thức review từ ít trang trọng nhất đến trang trọng nhất. Ai là người dẫn dắt buổi walkthrough và ai điều phối inspection?","expected_sources":["software-tesing-ISYS2092-SYS3397/Chapter 3 - Static Testings/Chapter 03 Static Testing.md"],"key_points":["informal review, walkthrough, technical review, inspection","a walkthrough is led by the author of the document","an inspection is led by a trained moderator and uses checklists and rules"],"answerable":true}
{"id":"static-cc-01","question":"How do you calculate cyclomatic complexity from a control flow graph, what quick shortcut can be used, and what value range counts as acceptable code?","expected_sources":["software-tesing-ISYS2092-SYS3397/Chapter 3 - Static Testings/Chapter 03 Static Testing.md"],"key_points":["CC = L - N + 2 (links minus nodes plus two)","shortcut: number of decision points plus one, or enclosed areas plus one","good code has CC between 1 and 10"],"answerable":true}
{"id":"tech-basis-01","question":"Ba nguồn cơ sở kiểm thử (test basis) là gì, và mỗi nguồn dẫn tới nhóm kỹ thuật thiết kế test nào?","expected_sources":["software-tesing-ISYS2092-SYS3397/Chapter 4 - Testing Techniques/01 - Test Techniques Overview (Tổng quan Kỹ thuật Kiểm thử).md"],"key_points":["specification leads to black-box (specification-based) techniques","structure leads to white-box (structure-based) techniques","knowledge or experience leads to experience-based techniques"],"answerable":true}
{"id":"blackbox-ep-01","question":"When I apply equivalence partitioning to an input that must lie in a numeric range, how many valid and invalid classes should I create, and how do I combine invalid classes into test cases?","expected_sources":["software-tesing-ISYS2092-SYS3397/Chapter 4 - Testing Techniques/02 - Black-Box - Specification-Based Testing.md"],"key_points":["a range gives one valid class and two invalid classes","each value belongs to exactly one partition and no partition is empty","valid classes are combined first; each further test case contains only one invalid class"],"answerable":true}
{"id":"blackbox-bva-01","question":"Với yêu cầu 10 ≤ x ≤ 20, phân tích giá trị biên kiểu 3 giá trị cần chọn những giá trị nào? Kiểu 2 giá trị khác ở đâu?","expected_sources":["software-tesing-ISYS2092-SYS3397/Chapter 4 - Testing Techniques/02 - Black-Box - Specification-Based Testing.md"],"key_points":["three-value BVA: 9, 10, 11 and 19, 20, 21","two-value BVA: 9, 10 and 20, 21","BVA assumes most defects sit at the boundaries"],"answerable":true}
{"id":"whitebox-01","question":"Why is white-box testing unable to reveal a requirement that was never implemented, and what does reaching 100% statement coverage actually mean?","expected_sources":["software-tesing-ISYS2092-SYS3397/Chapter 4 - Testing Techniques/03 - White-Box.md"],"key_points":["white-box tests are derived from the existing code structure, not the requirements specification","so missing implementation cannot be detected","100% statement coverage means every statement, including faulty ones, was executed at least once","decision coverage additionally needs every outcome (true and false) of each decision"],"answerable":true}
{"id":"combine-bb-wb-01","question":"Trong dự án thực tế, hộp đen và hộp trắng được kết hợp theo vòng lặp thế nào cho tới khi đạt tiêu chí thoát?","expected_sources":["software-tesing-ISYS2092-SYS3397/Chapter 4 - Testing Techniques/03 - White-Box.md","software-tesing-ISYS2092-SYS3397/Chapter 4 - Testing Techniques/04 - Thực tế kết hợp BlackBox và WhiteBox.md"],"key_points":["design the test specification and execute tests with a black-box technique","measure the code coverage reached with a white-box coverage technique","if coverage is below the target, add test cases and repeat","reaching the coverage target satisfies the exit criteria"],"answerable":true}
{"id":"exp-error-guessing-01","question":"What are the main weaknesses of error guessing as a test technique, and when is it normally applied?","expected_sources":["software-tesing-ISYS2092-SYS3397/Chapter 4 - Testing Techniques/05 - Experience - Based- Testing.md"],"key_points":["no plan and no documentation","coverage is unknown","defects are hard to reproduce and tests hard to repeat; no reusable testware","usually applied after structured techniques have reached coverage"],"answerable":true}
{"id":"exp-exploratory-01","question":"Test charter của một phiên kiểm thử thăm dò gồm những mục nào, và khi nào kiểm thử thăm dò là lựa chọn phù hợp?","expected_sources":["software-tesing-ISYS2092-SYS3397/Chapter 4 - Testing Techniques/05 - Experience - Based- Testing.md"],"key_points":["charter covers what, what not, why, how, expected problems and references","learning, test design and test execution happen at the same time","fits when specifications are missing, there is no time to script, fast feedback is needed or the project is agile"],"answerable":true}
{"id":"ch4-outline-01","question":"Which slide pages of the chapter 4 lecture deal with pair-wise testing and with state transition testing?","expected_sources":["software-tesing-ISYS2092-SYS3397/Chapter 4 - Testing Techniques/draft.md"],"key_points":["pair-wise testing is on pages 61–74","state transition testing is on pages 75–97"],"answerable":true}
{"id":"deviation-hypothesis-01","question":"Deviation hypothesis là gì, và một giả thuyết được viết tốt cần có những thành phần nào?","expected_sources":["software-tesing-ISYS2092-SYS3397/Terms-note/Deviation Hypothesis.md"],"key_points":["a structured prediction, written before testing, that the code deviates from a specific requirement (FR)","it is only a suspicion, not yet a defect","it names the violated FR, describes the deviation precisely and states the test that will verify it","if the test fails the hypothesis becomes a defect"],"answerable":true}
{"id":"qality-mapping-01","question":"When I move a standard test case into QAlity's limited fields, where should the prerequisites, test data and post-conditions go?","expected_sources":["software-tesing-ISYS2092-SYS3397/Tutorial - 3 - QAlity/Introduction-to-QAlity.md","software-tesing-ISYS2092-SYS3397/Tutorial - 3 - QAlity/Test-Management-with-QAlity.md"],"key_points":["test case ID and title go into the Summary field","prerequisites and test data go into the Description field","steps and expected results go into Test Steps","post-conditions and notes go into Comments"],"answerable":true}
{"id":"qality-vs-katalon-01","question":"Vì sao bài lab bắt dùng cả QAlity lẫn Katalon? Hai công cụ khác nhau thế nào?","expected_sources":["software-tesing-ISYS2092-SYS3397/Tutorial - 3 - QAlity/QAlity-vs-Katalon.md"],"key_points":["QAlity is a test management tool in Jira for manual testing and recording results","Katalon automates test scripts","not everything can be automated","QAlity covers planning, manual results and traceability from story to test case to bug"],"answerable":true}
{"id":"suite-vs-cycle-01","question":"In Jira with QAlity, what is the practical difference between a test suite and a test cycle?","expected_sources":["software-tesing-ISYS2092-SYS3397/Tutorial - 3 - QAlity/Test-case-vs-Test-Suite.md"],"key_points":["a test suite groups test cases by logic or function for organisation and long-term storage","a test cycle groups test cases to execute at a specific time","a cycle has start and end dates, an assignee and pass/fail results"],"answerable":true}
{"id":"qality-cycles-01","question":"How long should a hotfix test cycle take compared with a release test cycle, and what does each one focus on?","expected_sources":["software-tesing-ISYS2092-SYS3397/Tutorial - 3 - QAlity/Test-Management-with-QAlity.md"],"key_points":["hotfix cycle starts immediately and lasts 2–4 hours","hotfix only verifies the fixed bug","release cycle runs after code freeze for about one week","release cycle covers full regression and UAT"],"answerable":true}
{"id":"qality-fail-log-01","question":"Khi một test case bị fail, phần ghi nhận kết quả cần có những thông tin gì?","expected_sources":["software-tesing-ISYS2092-SYS3397/Tutorial - 3 - QAlity/Test-Management-with-QAlity.md"],"key_points":["status Failed with expected and actual results","a screenshot of the error","environment information such as browser and network","the test data used, the bug ID and the time"],"answerable":true}
{"id":"junit-01","question":"Which JUnit annotations set up and clean up before and after every test, and how does a JUnit test decide pass or fail?","expected_sources":["software-tesing-ISYS2092-SYS3397/Tutorial - W6 - Junit - 4/Introduction-JUnit.md"],"key_points":["@Test marks a test method","@Before/@BeforeEach sets up and @After/@AfterEach cleans up","assertions such as assertEquals or assertTrue compare actual with expected results"],"answerable":true}
{"id":"katalon-junit-01","question":"Tại sao lại chạy các bài test JUnit hộp trắng bên trong Katalon, vốn là công cụ kiểm thử hộp đen?","expected_sources":["software-tesing-ISYS2092-SYS3397/Tutorial - W6 - Junit - 4/Katalon-And-Junit.md"],"key_points":["Katalon can act as the runner for JUnit 4 and TestNG tests placed in Include/scripts/groovy","developer unit tests and QA tests are managed in one place","results are merged into one reporting dashboard","a single CI/CD run covers both"],"answerable":true}
{"id":"katalon-selfheal-01","question":"When should Katalon's self-healing be switched off, and how can I tell that a test passed only because self-healing stepped in?","expected_sources":["software-tesing-ISYS2092-SYS3397/Tutorial 1 - Get To Know Katalon/Katalon Self Healing.md"],"key_points":["turn it off while writing or debugging scripts so failures show immediately","turn it on for unattended runs such as CI or overnight suites","the log shows Passed together with an orange warning","configured under Project > Settings > Execution > Self-healing > Web UI"],"answerable":true}
{"id":"katalon-explorer-01","question":"Trong Katalon Studio, thư mục Object Repository và Profiles dùng để lưu gì?","expected_sources":["software-tesing-ISYS2092-SYS3397/Tutorial 1 - Get To Know Katalon/Overview Katalon interface.md"],"key_points":["Object Repository stores the identities of UI elements so they can be reused","Profiles store environment variables such as URL and credentials per environment","Test Suites group several test cases to run together"],"answerable":true}
{"id":"katalon-record-01","question":"What do you gain by recording steps in Katalon, and what information shows up in the execution report afterwards?","expected_sources":["software-tesing-ISYS2092-SYS3397/Tutorial 1 - Get To Know Katalon/Tại sao cần Report Steps.md"],"key_points":["recording quickly builds a test skeleton and fills the object repository","it bridges manual test cases to automation","report shows status Passed, Failed, Error or Incomplete","report includes step logs with elapsed time, the execution environment and error messages"],"answerable":true}
{"id":"katalon-export-01","question":"Làm sao để xuất báo cáo kết quả chạy test suite trong Katalon ra file PDF hoặc HTML?","expected_sources":["software-tesing-ISYS2092-SYS3397/Tutorial 1 - Get To Know Katalon/View and Export Test Report.md"],"key_points":["open the Reports folder in Tests Explorer and the test suite's folder","double-click the timestamped report to open it","use the export button at the top right and choose PDF or HTML"],"answerable":true}
{"id":"perf-types-01","question":"How do load, stress, spike and soak testing differ from each other?","expected_sources":["software-tesing-ISYS2092-SYS3397/W9 - Performance-Testing-with-JMeter/Introduction-to-Per-Testing.md"],"key_points":["load testing checks behaviour under the expected user load","stress testing pushes beyond expected load to find limits","spike testing checks reaction to a sudden surge in traffic","soak (endurance) testing runs over a long period"],"answerable":true}
{"id":"jmeter-plan-01","question":"Trong test plan của JMeter, Thread Group, Timer và CSV Data Set Config làm nhiệm vụ gì? Ramp-up period có nghĩa là gì?","expected_sources":["software-tesing-ISYS2092-SYS3397/W9 - Performance-Testing-with-JMeter/Introduction-to-Per-Testing.md"],"key_points":["Thread Group simulates concurrent virtual users (threads, ramp-up, loop count)","Timer adds delays (think time) between requests","CSV Data Set Config feeds data from CSV files for parameterisation","ramp-up period is the time JMeter takes to start all threads"],"answerable":true}
